	(text "Raspberry Pi Pico 2 W (RP2350). Library has no RP2350-specific\nsymbol yet; the RP2040 \"RaspberryPi_Pico\" module symbol is pin-\ncompatible (see MCU_Module library description) and used as-is.\nRUN, 3V3_EN and VBUS intentionally left unconnected (internally\npulled up / USB power unused) -- DESIGN.md SS3, SS5."
		(at 95 215 0)
		(effects (font (size 1.4 1.4)) (justify left))
		(uuid "cb5ee646-157d-449e-b7f2-db10a13e8b9c")
	)
	(text "RAIL POWER INPUT: guide-flag pickup braids (DESIGN.md SS7) --\nvariable analog DC, ~0-18V, proportional to throttle. NOT a\nfixed voltage."
		(at 35 66 0)
		(effects (font (size 1.4 1.4)) (justify left))
		(uuid "9ca224b2-6759-4b76-82fb-5488db84a5d2")
	)
	(text "Rear motor/drive section is kept stock (DESIGN.md SS7) --\ntapped from the same braid node, NOT through D1, so the\nmotor circuit is electrically untouched."
		(at 35 111 0)
		(effects (font (size 1.4 1.4)) (justify left))
		(uuid "07a81bab-01c9-43b5-b798-578f0fd71f4b")
	)
	(text "Buck-boost, Vin ~0.9-18V -> 5V regulated (feeds Pico VSYS, which\nthen supplies the Pico's own 3V3 rail to the sensors). EN tied to\nVIN = always enabled. Specific part not yet chosen -- DESIGN.md\nSS4 (e.g. TPS63070-class)."
		(at 150 68 0)
		(effects (font (size 1.4 1.4)) (justify left))
		(uuid "d47916f8-f2d1-4823-b703-ca03c33d9da8")
	)
	(text "Energy buffer on the REGULATED output rail, not the raw input --\nrides out low-throttle/contact-loss dips (SS4). R1+D2 limit charge\ninrush without penalizing discharge (D2 bypasses R1 when the cap is\nsupplying current). R1=4.7R and C1=1F sized together for a charge\ntime (5*R1*C1) of ~24s at power-up -- a 10F cap here would need\n~4 minutes to charge through R1; see SS4 before changing either\nvalue independently."
		(at 220 99.47 0)
		(effects (font (size 1.35 1.35)) (justify left))
		(uuid "8394bb5d-f736-46c7-9198-c5716a76aea2")
	)
	(text "PMW3360 breakout (DESIGN.md SS3). Generic 7-pin header shown --\nno breakout-specific symbol; pin order here is documentation only\n(each net is wired by label, not by physical pin position).\nMotion sensor lens standoff/focus height: DESIGN.md SS7."
		(at 40 181 0)
		(effects (font (size 1.4 1.4)) (justify left))
		(uuid "881db5b8-f94a-4788-9b2f-98436d0692f1")
	)
	(text "ICM-42688-P breakout (DESIGN.md SS3). Gyro+accel only -- no\nmagnetometer, deliberately (motor-magnet interference, SS3).\nGeneric 5-pin header shown, wired by label."
		(at 40 234 0)
		(effects (font (size 1.4 1.4)) (justify left))
		(uuid "92923ced-1dde-4453-ab9d-fea96972a34c")
	)
	(text "IR reflectance lap-trigger sensor (DESIGN.md SS6). Generic\n3-pin header shown, wired by label. Reads a contrast marker\nat the start/finish line."
		(at 310 157 0)
		(effects (font (size 1.4 1.4)) (justify left))
		(uuid "425c75f9-8e1d-430d-9385-ee08386a2e49")
	)
	(text "SLOT CAR TRACK MAPPER -- SYSTEM ELECTRICAL SCHEMATIC"
		(at 40 15 0)
		(effects (font (size 2.5 2.5)) (justify left))
		(uuid "79cc2546-e3fe-42de-a592-61b77825e910")
	)
	(text "Single top-level sheet, all components. See DESIGN.md for the full design rationale.\nNet-name labels (not direct wires) join same-named connections across the sheet --\ne.g. every \"GND\" power symbol and every \"SPI0_SCK\" label are one electrical net."
		(at 40 22 0)
		(effects (font (size 1.3 1.3)) (justify left))
		(uuid "b6c0e20b-7e0d-41ec-9dfc-03ee41658f18")
	)
)
